Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: qcom: rpmhpd: don't clamp GMU-managed rails pre-sync_state

Ported from ROCKNIX/distribution's own
0121-pmdomain-qcom-rpmhpd-no-max-clamp-on-gmu-rails.patch (SM8550
device patch set). Marks gfx/gmxc state_synced from boot so pre-sync
votes use the real lowest corner instead of an inflated safety clamp.
These rails carry no bootloader state and have no other consumers, so
the clamp protects nothing on them - it only holds the Adreno 740 GPU
(RP6, AYN Odin 2, AYANEO Pocket ACE/DMG/S2K) to an artificially high
minimum power-domain corner until genpd's state sync completes early
in boot.

Complements 0120 (GPU_CC power-domain plumbing in the DTS, already in
this tree) rather than conflicting with it - that patch describes the
power-domain wiring in sm8550.dtsi, this one changes the driver's
pre-sync_state clamping behavior for those same two rails.

Context (struct rpmhpd gfx/gmxc definitions) verified against current
torvalds/linux drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmhpd.c - identical field layout,
no existing armada patch touches this file.
---
diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmhpd.c b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmhpd.c
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmhpd.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmhpd.c
@@ -120,6 +120,7 @@ static struct rpmhpd gbx = {
 static struct rpmhpd gfx = {
 	.pd = { .name = "gfx", },
 	.res_name = "gfx.lvl",
+	.state_synced = true,
 };

 static struct rpmhpd lcx = {
@@ -225,6 +226,7 @@ static struct rpmhpd qphy = {
 static struct rpmhpd gmxc = {
 	.pd = { .name = "gmxc", },
 	.res_name = "gmxc.lvl",
+	.state_synced = true,
 };

 /* Eliza RPMH powerdomains */
